# PART 8 — MULTIPLE WORKFORCE ASSIGNMENTS PER PROJECT

This is an important project management correction.

Inside every project's "Assign Workforce Member" section, the authorised user must be able to add any number of workforce members.

The current interface must not restrict the user to adding just one workforce member.

## Required user experience

The workflow should be:

1. Open a project.
2. Click Assign Workforce Member.
3. Select an employee or approved artisan.
4. Confirm assignment.
5. The person appears in the project's assigned workforce list.
6. The user can immediately click Add Another.
7. Select another workforce member.
8. Repeat as many times as necessary.

The assignment interface should support multiple additions without closing or resetting the entire project form unnecessarily.

Provide:

- Search.
- Employee/artisan selection.
- Role display.
- Department display.
- Assignment date.
- Assigned responsibility.
- Assignment status.
- Removal or reassignment through authorised controls.

Prevent duplicate active assignments of the same workforce member to the same project unless the existing architecture explicitly supports multiple assignment periods.

## A. Workforce visibility

Every assigned workforce member must be able to see the project on their own dashboard, according to their role and permissions.

For example:

- Site Supervisor sees operational project details.
- Technical Officer sees inspection and QC responsibilities.
- Procurement sees authorised procurement information.
- Admin sees workforce and administrative information.
- Accounts sees relevant financial and verified operational information.
- Management sees organisation-wide information.

Being assigned to a project must not automatically grant unrestricted access to the entire project or company database.

## B. Database integrity

Use the existing project workforce assignment structure if available.

Otherwise, implement a proper many-to-many relationship between projects and workforce members.

Each assignment must identify:

- Project ID.
- Employee or workforce member ID.
- Assigned role or responsibility.
- Assigned by.
- Assignment date.
- Assignment status.
- Removal or reassignment information where applicable.

Ensure that project membership is respected by RLS policies.

All assigned employees must be able to retrieve the appropriate assigned projects through their authenticated accounts.

